  "body": "## What\n\n`crates/app/tests/operations.rs` generates every operation through the app layer, so its tests pin\nthe motion generators end to end — but its Gate map named `app::` modules only. A change under\n`crates/motion/src/multiaxis/` therefore selected no suite that drives multiaxis rough end to end,\nso `cargo xtask gate quick` could pass while\n`multiaxis_rough_refuses_a_slot_the_cone_cannot_clear` sat out. PR #1044 hit exactly that: its gate\ncame out green and the failure surfaced only when a stacked merge ran the whole app list.\n\n## The fix\n\n- `operations.rs`'s Gate map names the generators its tests drive end to end:\n  `motion::machining2d`, `motion::machining3d`, `motion::drilling`, `motion::finishing3d`,\n  `motion::multiaxis`, `motion::plunge_law`.\n- An xtask unit test pins both halves against this checkout: the map names every one of them, and a\n  plan for `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/mod.rs` selects `app:operations`. A header that loses a name\n  now fails in xtask's own suite instead of in a later PR's gate run.\n\n## Process\n\n`xtask/src/tests.rs` is a process file, so `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` goes 16 → 17 (the same number\nas the other open process PRs; whichever merges second renumbers on its merge of main).\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo test -p xtask` — 34 passed (new test included)\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` — ok (app operations suite 49 s, xtask 2 s)\n- Selection proof: with a one-line probe under `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/`,\n  `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main --plan` lists `app suites ... --test operations`;\n  before the header change it listed motion suites only.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` — clean\n\n## Merge note\n\n#965, #967, #972 and #1033 each rewrite the same `Gate map (M4.4)` line of `operations.rs` and\nalready name some of these modules. Whichever lands first, the other keeps both sets of names —\nhere `motion::machining3d`, `motion::multiaxis` and `motion::plunge_law` are the additions this PR\nbrings. The new xtask test catches a lost name.\n\nChangelog: none\nFixes #1068\n",
